  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Eating a healthy, plant-based diet doesn’t mean depriving yourself of sweet treats! Dates are a great whole-food sweetener. Try them in these delicious Oatmeal Cookie Dough Bites. They come together easily in a food processor for a quick and simple sweet snack. Get the free recipe </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/oatmeal-cookie-dough-bites/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and check out our Instagram for </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CRkIVezpvho/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">a video</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on how they are made.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> </span></p>\n<h4>Key Takeaways: Blood Pressure</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-73264\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/BP-Meter.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/BP-Meter.png 600w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/BP-Meter-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/BP-Meter-540x540.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>According to the renowned Global Burden of Disease Study, high blood pressure is the leading risk factor for death in the world by contributing to various causes of mortality. So, what can we do to keep our blood pressure down? Check out the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/blood-pressure/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for a summary and videos like </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die-from-high-blood-pressure/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Die from High Blood Pressure</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-lower-blood-pressure-naturally-with-lifestyle-changes/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Lower Blood Pressure Naturally</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Volume 57 Out Now</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-84939 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-1024x1024.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-1024x1024.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-960x960.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-1536x1536.jpeg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-500x500.jpeg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-1200x1200.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-720x720.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork-540x540.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/vol-57-artwork.jpeg 2000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>My new volume of videos is out now. This collection includes an update on bovine leukemia virus and breast cancer, a series on longevity, potassium chloride as a salt substitute, and much more.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each video in this new volume will be released online over the next few months, available for free, of course, but if you don’t want to wait, you can watch all of them by streaming </span><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">right now</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you are a $25+ monthly supporter, you’re likely already an expert on these new topics by now, since you already received a complimentary link to the new download. If you’d like early access to new videos before they’re available to the public, please consider becoming a </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/?mc_cid=1b9efb2a80&amp;mc_eid=[UNIQID]/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">monthly supporter</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Without your generosity, we wouldn’t be able to continue our work.</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Thank you!</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Volunteer Translators Needed</h4>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"YouTube video player\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/4BwITF2uJvA\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"></iframe></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you watch our videos on </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NutritionFacts.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> or </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/NutritionFactsOrg\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">YouTube</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, you can access captions in several different languages by clicking on the settings wheel in the lower-right corner of the video. All of our videos are in English and have translated subtitles. They are viewed in nearly every country in the world! If you have a background in professional translation, please consider applying </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/translators/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We are especially seeking translators for: Dutch, French, German, Hindi, Hungarian, Italian, Simplified Chinese, Russian, Spanish, Tamil, and Vietnamese.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Volunteer Spotlight: Xiaoju Zhang</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-73262 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/1-e1645129757665-1024x965.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"212\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/1-e1645129757665-1024x965.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/1-e1645129757665-960x904.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/1-e1645129757665-768x723.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/1-e1645129757665-1200x1130.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/1-e1645129757665-720x678.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/1-e1645129757665-540x509.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/02/1-e1645129757665.jpg 1621w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 212px) 100vw, 212px\"/>“I translate the videos and other content from English to Chinese. I enjoy working with the NutritionFacts.org team while learning healthy diet facts. I hope what we do here can help more people find their own paths to a healthy lifestyle. My favorite healthy food is tofu: The possibilities are unlimited!”</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-60211 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/foods-that-cause-inflammation/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70731\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Milk, cottage cheese, sour cream and wheat on rustic wooden background\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/56-16-Which-Foods-are-Pro-Inflammatory.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/foods-that-cause-inflammation/\"><b>Foods That Cause Inflammation</b></a><b> </b></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Inflammatory markers can double within six hours of eating a pro-inflammatory meal. Which foods are the worst?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/fighting-the-ten-hallmarks-of-cancer-with-food/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70337\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Plant foods high in fiber with whole wheat pasta, nuts, fruit and vegetables on a rustic background\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/56-14-Fighting-the-Ten-Hallmarks-of-Cancer-with-Food.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/fighting-the-ten-hallmarks-of-cancer-with-food/\"><b>Fighting the Ten Hallmarks of Cancer with Food</b></a><b> </b></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The foundation of cancer prevention is plants, not pills.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-dr-gregers-daily-dozen-checklist/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-70560\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"painting with Dr. Greger’s Daily Dozen recommendations\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/1-Dr.-Gregers-Daily-Dozen-Checklist.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-dr-gregers-daily-dozen-checklist/\"><b>Flashback Friday: Dr. Greger’s Daily Dozen Checklist</b></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In my book </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Die</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, I center my recommendations around a Daily Dozen checklist of all the things I try to fit into my daily routine.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
